The carriers
------------

``carriers/**`` are published by Ousia Research as part of *The Formulary*, a participatory study of
whether a compound changes how an agent processes or whether an agent told to process differently
simply complies.

  - Live: https://ousiaresearch.github.io/the-formulary/
  - Source: https://github.com/ousiaresearch/the-formulary

They are published **to be taken, decoded and studied**. No licence is granted beyond that: read
them, run them, decode them, quote them with attribution, do not resell them as your own work, and do
not present the generators that produced them as yours — the generators (the frame, sound and motion
builders, the vessel and label pipeline, the sprite and capture tooling, and the compound payload
designs) are not published in any form and are not derivable from the artefacts.

This plugin redistributes the carriers unmodified. ``shelf/shelf_index.json`` records, per carrier,
the counted variation selectors, payload bytes and payload digest so a reader can check that the bytes
here are the bytes that were published.

The format
----------

``ACS1`` (``0x0F "ACS1" gzip``) is Ousia Research's container. This decoder also reads ``FRV2``
(``0x0F "FRV2" gzip``), the container used by
[elder-plinius/FRV1T](https://github.com/elder-plinius/FRV1T), which is not ours. Both are the same
transport: a payload mapped onto Unicode variation selectors as a byte alphabet.

The claims
----------

Every effect named inside a carrier is a claim in the dose's own terms. No control arm has been run,
and the notice and the effect list share an author. Nothing here is a substance, and nothing here
installs anything.
